---
import { pageDates } from "../page-dates.js";
import PageLayout from "../layouts/PageLayout.astro";
import { SITE, AUTHOR } from "../site.config.js";
---
<PageLayout
  title="Editorial Policy"
  description={`How ${SITE.name} writes, checks and updates its calculators and guides, how AI tools are used, and how corrections are handled.`}
  updated={pageDates("/editorial-policy/").updated ?? pageDates("/editorial-policy/").published}
>
  <p>{SITE.name} is run by <a href={`/author/${AUTHOR.slug}/`}>{AUTHOR.name}</a>, who is responsible for what is published. This page explains how the calculators and guides are made and checked, including the part automation plays.</p>

  <h2>What we publish</h2>
  <p>Calculators for estimating materials, and guides that explain how to measure, what the numbers mean and what to watch for. We only publish a guide when it adds something a reader can use: a worked example, a table, a diagram or a clear answer to a specific question.</p>

  <h2>How numbers are checked</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Formulas are published on the <a href="/methodology/">methodology page</a>.</li>
    <li>Calculator code has automated tests with hand-worked examples. Formulas are verified by those tests and by code, not by outside experts.</li>
    <li>New guides pass automated quality checks before they go live (length, structure, leftover draft text, complete sentences, description length). These checks catch many problems but not every wrong number, so guides can contain errors.</li>
    <li>Where a guide quotes a building-code limit or a manufacturer figure, it links to the source it relies on. Where we cannot name a source, the text should say the figure is a typical value and not a rule.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>The site has no peer review, no professional certification and no licensed-engineer sign-off, and nothing on it should be read as claiming any.</p>

  <h2>Use of AI tools</h2>
  <p>Many guides were first drafted with an AI language model, then checked by automated rules and corrected by the author. Automatic daily publishing is switched off: new guides are published only after the author has reviewed them. In November 2026 every published guide was re-audited for wording, tables, arithmetic and sources, and a guide with a wrong formula was taken down and rewritten. Any error found later is fixed and the page shows an updated date. The calculators are written and tested by hand.</p>

  <h2>Independence</h2>
  <p>{SITE.name} is independent. No manufacturer or retailer pays for coverage or reviews pages before publication. The site may show advertising; advertisers have no say in the content. If we ever add affiliate links, pages that contain them will say so.</p>

  <h2>Updates and corrections</h2>
  <p>Each page shows the date it was last updated, and that date changes only when the content does. If a guide contains a mistake, we correct it and record the correction with its date on the page. To report an error, email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> or use the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p>
</PageLayout>
